      "message": "please establish the failure case you are solving here can actually happen. Just because the offset is returned from `lseek` does not mean it can be different from the offset that was passed in.\n\n```\noff_t offset \u003d n;\nstatic_assert(n \u003e\u003d 0);\n\noff_t ret \u003d lseek(fd, offset, SEEK_SET);\n\nassert(ret !\u003d offset \u0026\u0026 ret \u003e\u003d 0);\n```\n\nTo establish the possibility of this failure case you could refer to kernel source code or sections of\n https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/lseek.2.html",
