      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for requesting evidence. The /dev/null test does not establish this failure case for an EEPROM sysfs file. \nI checked the at24/NVMEM path: the EEPROM attribute has no custom seek callback, so sysfs uses generic_file_llseek, which returns the requested offset on successful SEEK_SET. \nThe existing code already handles failed seeks. I cannot substantiate the claimed EEPROM failure, so this patch is not justified and I propose withdrawing it.\n\nReference: https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/lseek.2.html",
